    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1357">

                <pb facs="1220" n="962" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg962"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1536</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-02T20:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1915, 8 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 3, 8 a. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>467. Your 434.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1357-f1"/> Brought contents to the attention
                    of the Foreign Office. The Grand Vizier who seemed to disapprove threats of
                    military commander told me he would speak to Minister of War. The latter wrote
                    me that fourth army corps commander asks four thousand pounds Turkish as
                    indemnity for families of persons killed. I replied Minister of War that this is
                    excessive and certainly not <pb facs="1221" n="963" xml:id="pg963"/> nominal, as
                    he had told me it would be. Have directed consul at Alexandretta to investigate
                    matter from neutral point of view.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
